From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:21:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] libfetch: include 400 and 599 in HTTP_ERROR()

HTTP_ERROR() excluded both ends of its intended range, so 400 (Bad
Request) and 599 were not recognised as errors.  http_request() then
fell through to its redirect handling for such a response, and would
follow it if the error carried a Location header.
---
 libfetch/http.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libfetch/http.c b/libfetch/http.c
index d57d8e8..63d8d33 100644
--- a/libfetch/http.c
+++ b/libfetch/http.c
@@ -104,7 +104,7 @@
 			    || (xyz) == HTTP_TEMP_REDIRECT \
 			    || (xyz) == HTTP_SEE_OTHER)
 
-#define HTTP_ERROR(xyz) ((xyz) > 400 && (xyz) < 599)
+#define HTTP_ERROR(xyz) ((xyz) >= 400 && (xyz) < 600)
 
 static int http_cmd(conn_t *, const char *, ...) LIBFETCH_PRINTFLIKE(2, 3);
 
